{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat AGENTS.md\nsed -n '1,48p' scripts/reconstruction_v1.py\nsed -n '286,345p' scripts/reconstruction_v1.py\"","aggregated_output":"# AccDSL project instructions\n\n## Mission entry point\n\nBefore substantive work in this project, read:\n\n1. [Mission control](MISSION_CONTROL.md).\n2. [Requirements and acceptance evidence](docs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md).\n3. [Current checkpoint](docs/plans/accounting-product-design-checkpoint.md).\n4. The gap records relevant to the task:\n   [initial audit](docs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md) and\n   [expanded mission audit](docs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md).\n5. For the authorised master-program work, read the\n   [master checkpoint](docs/plans/accounting-master-checkpoint.md), executable\n   phase catalog and current `data/accounting-master/next-plan.md`. The older\n   corpus checkpoint remains historical evidence; current phase execution is\n   recorded by the master without rewriting frozen release hashes.\n\nThe mission preserves the user's goals across sessions. Current user directions\nand higher-priority instructions still control. Local documents must not be\nused to request fresh permission for work already authorised by the user.\n\n## Working rules\n\n- Identify the MC requirements addressed by each nontrivial plan or work unit.\n  Audit the plan before implementation, experiments or long diagnostics.\n- Preserve the full goals while staging execution. A small financing demo,\n  clean PDF build or six populated research ledgers cannot close requirements\n  for whole-company representation, research quality or implementation detail.\n- Distinguish direct user requirements, policy requirements and derived\n  engineering choices. Do not silently convert a convenient library, model\n  assumption or stage boundary into an immutable product requirement.\n- Keep source evidence, interpretations, assumptions, joint history families\n  and scenario-specific results separate and traceable. Preserve unknowns;\n  do not invent facts, probabilities, accounting compliance or completeness.\n- Close gaps with the specified evidence, and update the requirements register\n  and checkpoint after meaningful changes. Add newly discovered gaps rather\n  than treating the current list as exhaustive.\n- Follow the applicable policies under\n  `/home/chakwong/python/claudecodex/policies`. Preserve unrelated work and the\n  original paper collection. The existing `.git` marker is not a usable\n  repository; do not initialise or commit merely to create provenance.\n- Keep operational mission/checklist material out of the reader-facing\n  scholarly narrative unless it serves a real implementation-reference purpose.\n- Apply MC35, the user's internal-preparation-before-paid-review requirement.\n  Finish feasible source research, facts, calculations, software checks and\n  document repairs before referring a specific question to a professional.\n  Supply a proposed answer, exact sources, competing interpretation and checked\n  consequences. Keep unfinished internal work on the internal queue; “human\n  review pending” is an acceptance status, not a reason to stop that work.\n  Ordinary reader feedback need not be purchased from an accounting firm.\n  No professional engagement, outreach or fees are authorised by this policy.\n  See `docs/design/review/internal-before-expert.md` and the current checkpoint.\n\nThe current manuscript is specification-incomplete. Read the checkpoint and\nrequirements before resuming from an older note that says only final review\nremains. This file authorises no autonomous background campaign or external\npublication; it directs work undertaken under the user's active instructions.\n\"\"\"Declared-template reconstruction and bounded uncertainty operations, version 1.\"\"\"\nfrom copy import deepcopy\nfrom fractions import Fraction as F\nimport hashlib\nimport json\nimport z3\nfrom rational_solver_v1 import (Problem, Budget, UnsupportedFragment, q, rational, domain_formula,\n                                disclosure_domain, half_even, solve)\n\n\nADMISSION_FIELDS = {\n    'ExtractionReading': ('source', 'locator', 'review_decision'),\n    'HistoricalFact': ('evidence', 'reason'),\n    'AccountingElection': ('package', 'permitted_treatments', 'election', 'effective_date', 'eligibility_evidence'),\n    'MeasurementEstimate': ('method', 'measurement_date', 'inputs'),\n    'BehaviourPolicy': ('policy', 'information_set', 'decision_time'),\n    'FutureInnovation': ('driver', 'future_period', 'scenario', 'joint_law', 'measure'),\n}\n\n\ndef admit(record):\n    kind = record.get('kind')\n    if kind not in ADMISSION_FIELDS:\n        raise ValueError('unknown uncertainty category')\n    for key in ('id', 'scope', 'provenance', 'dependencies') + ADMISSION_FIELDS[kind]:\n        if key not in record or (key != 'dependencies' and not record[key]):\n            raise ValueError('missing admission field: ' + key)\n    if not isinstance(record['dependencies'], list) or not isinstance(record['provenance'], list):\n        raise ValueError('dependencies and provenance must be explicit lists')\n    if kind == 'ExtractionReading' and record['review_decision'] != 'Accept':\n        raise ValueError('extraction reading is not accepted')\n    if kind == 'AccountingElection' and record['election'] not in record['permitted_treatments']:\n        raise ValueError('treatment not permitted by declared package')\n    return deepcopy(record)\n\n\ndef expression(node, env):\n    if isinstance(node, bool):\n        return z3.BoolVal(node)\n    if isinstance(node, (str, int, F)):\n        return env[node] if isinstance(node, str) and node in env else q(node)\n    if not isinstance(node, list) or not node:\n        raise ValueError('expression must be exact scalar, reference or operation list')\n    op, *args = node\n    args = [expression(x, env) for x in args]\n    ops = {'+': lambda a,b:a+b, '-': lambda a,b:a-b, '*': lambda a,b:a*b,\n           '/': lambda a,b:a/b, '==': lambda a,b:a==b, '<=': lambda a,b:a<=b,\n           '>=': lambda a,b:a>=b, '<': lambda a,b:a<b, '>': lambda a,b:a>b,\ndef group_contracts(contracts, scenario, horizon, previous=None):\n    \"\"\"Exact additive simple-debt grouping; retain full constituent memory.\"\"\"\n    request={'contracts':contracts,'scenario':scenario,'horizon':horizon}\n    signature=hashlib.sha256(json.dumps(request,sort_keys=True).encode()).hexdigest()\n    if previous and previous['signature']!=signature:raise ValueError('grouping requires revalidation')\n    if not contracts or horizon[0]>=horizon[1]:raise ValueError('invalid grouping request')\n    if len({c['id'] for c in contracts}) != len(contracts):\n        raise ValueError('duplicate contract identity would double-count principal')\n    allowed = {'id', 'principal', 'rate', 'reset', 'maturity', 'hedge'}\n    if any(set(c) != allowed or c['hedge'] != 'none' or c['reset'] not in ('fixed','floating')\n           or rational(c['principal']) < 0 for c in contracts):\n        raise UnsupportedFragment('only nonnegative unhedged bullet debt is supported')\n    keys=('rate','reset','maturity','hedge')\n    if any(tuple(c[k] for k in keys)!=tuple(contracts[0][k] for k in keys) for c in contracts):\n        raise UnsupportedFragment('different contract memory keys')\n    if any(c['maturity']<=horizon[1] for c in contracts):raise UnsupportedFragment('maturity inside horizon')\n    rate=rational(scenario['rate'] if contracts[0]['reset']=='floating' else contracts[0]['rate'])\n    year_fraction=rational(scenario['year_fraction'])\n    if year_fraction <= 0:\n        raise ValueError('positive declared horizon year fraction required')\n    principal=sum((rational(c['principal']) for c in contracts),F(0))\n    individual=sum((rational(c['principal'])*rate*year_fraction for c in contracts),F(0))\n    grouped=principal*rate*year_fraction\n    if individual!=grouped:raise ValueError('additivity check failed')\n    return {'signature':signature,'status':'ExactForDeclaredAdditiveProfile','memory':deepcopy(contracts),\n            'scenario':deepcopy(scenario),'horizon':list(horizon),'principal':str(principal),\n            'interest':str(grouped),'transition_preserved':True,'report_preserved':True}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
