{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat docs/design/fixtures/temporal.json\nsed -n '154,170p' scripts/check_repair_conformance.py\nsed -n '413,437p' scripts/core0_ir_v1.py\nsed -n '560,592p' scripts/core0_ir_v1.py\"","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"availability_policy\": \"date-only filing is available at next midnight in stated reporting timezone\",\n  \"assertions\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"h1-original\",\n      \"key\": \"revenue:H1:USD:NS:Demo\",\n      \"value\": \"120\",\n      \"available\": \"2024-08-01T00:00:00Z\",\n      \"ingested\": \"2024-08-03T00:00:00Z\",\n      \"vintage\": \"v1\",\n      \"supersedes\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"h1-restated\",\n      \"key\": \"revenue:H1:USD:NS:Demo\",\n      \"value\": \"110\",\n      \"available\": \"2025-03-02T00:00:00Z\",\n      \"ingested\": \"2025-03-05T00:00:00Z\",\n      \"vintage\": \"v2\",\n      \"supersedes\": [\n        \"h1-original\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"fy\",\n      \"key\": \"revenue:FY:USD:NS:Demo\",\n      \"value\": \"260\",\n      \"available\": \"2025-03-02T00:00:00Z\",\n      \"ingested\": \"2025-03-05T00:00:00Z\",\n      \"vintage\": \"v2\",\n      \"supersedes\": []\n    }\n  ],\n  \"queries\": [\n    {\n      \"cutoff\": \"2024-09-01T00:00:00Z\",\n      \"system_as_of\": null,\n      \"expect\": [\n        \"h1-original\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"cutoff\": \"2025-03-03T00:00:00Z\",\n      \"system_as_of\": null,\n      \"expect\": [\n        \"h1-restated\",\n        \"fy\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"cutoff\": \"2025-03-03T00:00:00Z\",\n      \"system_as_of\": \"2025-03-04T00:00:00Z\",\n      \"expect\": [\n        \"h1-original\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"cutoff\": \"2025-03-06T00:00:00Z\",\n      \"system_as_of\": null,\n      \"mode\": \"original\",\n      \"expect\": [\n        \"h1-original\",\n        \"fy\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"expected_valid_h2\": \"150\",\n  \"incompatible_vintage_h2\": \"140 must be rejected\"\n}\ndef temporal():\n    f=load('temporal.json')\n    for i,q in enumerate(f['queries']):\n        eligible=[a for a in f['assertions'] if a['available']<=q['cutoff'] and (q.get('system_as_of') is None or a['ingested']<=q['system_as_of'])]\n        if q.get('mode')=='original':eligible=[a for a in eligible if not a['supersedes']]\n        else:\n            superseded={x for a in eligible for x in a['supersedes']};eligible=[a for a in eligible if a['id'] not in superseded]\n        check('temporal_query_'+str(i),{a['id'] for a in eligible}==set(q['expect']),q)\n    check('restated_half_year',Q('260')-Q('110')==Q(f['expected_valid_h2']),'Original H1 has incompatible vintage; its subtraction is not a current-view H2')\n\ndef sector_checks():\n    f=load('sectors.json');b=f['bank'];o={k:Q(v) for k,v in b['opening'].items()};e={k:Q(v) for k,v in b['events'].items()}\n    a=dict(cash=o['cash']-e['external_transfer']+e['loan_interest_cash'],gross_loans=o['gross_loans']+e['origination'],allowance=e['allowance_target'],deposits=o['deposits']+e['origination']-e['external_transfer']+e['deposit_interest_accrued'],equity=o['equity']+e['loan_interest_cash']-e['deposit_interest_accrued']-(e['allowance_target']-o['allowance']))\n    compare('bank_before_runoff',a,b['expected_before_runoff'])\n    check('bank_funding',max(Q(0),Q(b['runoff'])-a['cash'])==Q(b['expected_draw'])<=Q(b['facility_limit']),'Draw 4 to settle runoff 25')\n    check('bank_default_retained',Q(b['default_runoff'])-a['cash']-Q(b['facility_limit'])==Q(b['expected_unpaid']),'Unpaid 9 is an economic default outcome')\n    check('bank_capital',a['equity']-Q(b['regulatory_deduction'])==Q(b['expected_CET1']) and a['gross_loans']*Q(b['risk_weight'])==Q(b['expected_RWA']),'Illustrative prudential assumptions, no Basel compliance claim')\nclass ReadingBinding:\n    key: str\n    literal: str\n    amount: Fraction | int | str\n    currency: str\n    instant: str\n    uri: str\n    filing_id: str\n    available: str\n    ingested: str\n    reviewer: str\n    review_date: str\n    review_reason: str\n    cutoff: str\n    system_as_of: Optional[str] = None\n    prior_view: str = \"fixture:empty-view\"\n    extraction: str = \"provided-binding\"\n    action: Optional[str] = None\n\n    def __post_init__(self):\n        object.__setattr__(self, \"amount\", _fraction(self.amount))\n\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\nclass OpeningBinding:\nclass CompileBindings:\n    packages: tuple[PackageBinding, ...] = ()\n    readings: tuple[ReadingBinding, ...] = ()\n    openings: tuple[OpeningBinding, ...] = ()\n    reports: tuple[ReportBinding, ...] = ()\n    assumptions: tuple[AssumptionBinding, ...] = ()\n    calendar_id: str = \"DemoCalendar@1\"\n    calendar_name: str = \"Gregorian\"\n    horizon_start: str = \"2026-01-01\"\n    horizon_end: str = \"2027-01-01\"\n    symbol_uncertainty: str = \"HistoricalFact\"\n    entity_perimeter: str = \"Acme-only\"\n    admissions: tuple[SymbolAdmission, ...] = ()\n    alternatives: tuple[AlternativeBinding, ...] = ()\n\n    def __init__(self, packages: Sequence[PackageBinding] = (), readings: Sequence[ReadingBinding] = (),\n                 openings: Sequence[OpeningBinding] = (), reports: Sequence[ReportBinding] = (),\n                 assumptions: Sequence[AssumptionBinding] = (), calendar_id: Optional[str] = None,\n                 calendar_name: Optional[str] = None, horizon_start: Optional[str] = None,\n                 horizon_end: Optional[str] = None, symbol_uncertainty: Optional[str] = None,\n                 entity_perimeter: Optional[str] = None, admissions: Sequence[SymbolAdmission] = (),\n                 alternatives: Sequence[AlternativeBinding] = ()):\n        object.__setattr__(self, \"packages\", tuple(packages))\n        object.__setattr__(self, \"readings\", tuple(readings))\n        object.__setattr__(self, \"openings\", tuple(openings))\n        object.__setattr__(self, \"reports\", tuple(reports))\n        object.__setattr__(self, \"assumptions\", tuple(assumptions))\n        object.__setattr__(self, \"calendar_id\", calendar_id)\n        object.__setattr__(self, \"calendar_name\", calendar_name)\n        object.__setattr__(self, \"horizon_start\", horizon_start)\n        object.__setattr__(self, \"horizon_end\", horizon_end)\n        object.__setattr__(self, \"symbol_uncertainty\", symbol_uncertainty)\n        object.__setattr__(self, \"entity_perimeter\", entity_perimeter)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg --files data/accounting-master | rg 'source-work-register.json\"'$'\"'\nrg -n '\"'^##? .*G1[23456]|G12|G13|G14|G15|G16'\"' docs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md\nsed -n '1,42p' MISSION_CONTROL.md\nsed -n '1,24p' docs/plans/accounting-master-checkpoint.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg --files data/accounting-master | rg 'source-work-register.json\"'$'\"'\nrg -n '\"'^##? .*G1[23456]|G12|G13|G14|G15|G16'\"' docs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md\nsed -n '1,42p' MISSION_CONTROL.md\nsed -n '1,24p' docs/plans/accounting-master-checkpoint.md\"","aggregated_output":"data/accounting-master/runs/20261002T180732-83972f09/P01/source-work-register.json\ndata/accounting-master/runs/preflight-20261002/P01/source-work-register.json\n60:### G12. Cross-company concepts and aggregation need formal mapping semantics\n79:### G13. Multiple clocks are identified without complete historical query rules\n98:### G14. Scenario modes and permitted information need enforceable contracts\n119:### G15. Different kinds of uncertainty need different admissibility rules\n138:### G16. Aggregation and history compression need a practical resolution policy\n# AccDSL mission control\n\nEstablished 2 October 2026 (Asia/Hong_Kong) at the user's request.\nStatus: active mission; Version 1.2 is a repaired design candidate with checked\nreference cases. Full product, domain and human acceptance remain pending.\n\n## Purpose\n\nDesign a system that represents a company's historical financial disclosures,\npreserves economically different histories and interpretations compatible with\nthe evidence, and carries those alternatives into scenario-dependent future\njournals and financial statements. Preserve their separate conditional outcome\ndistributions or feasible sets, including uncertainty that cannot be assigned\ndefensible probabilities.\n\nThe immediate deliverable is a detailed, readable LaTeX product and method\ndesign, with compiled PDF, supporting literature and software investigation,\nprecise implementation contracts and acceptance examples. The eventual product\nis the working representation and simulation engine. A document build, a small\nfinancing example and an implemented prototype are different achievements.\n\n## Authority and origin\n\nThis mission records the user's existing directions; it does not replace new\nuser instructions or higher-priority instructions. The three original requests\nare preserved in saved session `01a0f8e0-0c0b-7332-8f7e-d6b93ce32761`, at JSONL\nrecords 10, 115 and 145. They establish whole-company history, heterogeneous\naccounting, preservation of alternative journals/outcomes, a broad literature\nand software survey, and an implementation-governing LaTeX document. The current\nrequest establishes this durable mission and a requirements-based gap audit.\n\nThe user's subsequent direction establishes MC35: complete feasible internal\npreparation before paying for professional review. The user supplied a planning\nrate of US$500–1,200/hour. This work order is binding; no estimated savings or\nprofessional engagement is inferred from it.\n\nThe [requirements register](docs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md)\ndistinguishes direct user requirements from policy obligations and engineering\nrequirements derived from those goals. Python, storage engines, parser design,\nsolver libraries and a particular first-company example remain replaceable\nimplementation proposals. Designing a DSL is part of the work; claiming it is\nbetter than all alternatives is not a predetermined conclusion.\n# Accounting master checkpoint\n\nUpdated 3 October 2026, Hong Kong, during run `20261002T233421-cea9e631`.\nThe user's create/review/execute instruction and original standing grant remain\nactive. The catalog preserves all MC01–MC35 and G1–G18, with no missing IDs.\n\n## Active run and next action\n\nTool session `78463` is running. P00–P04 are accepted internally; P05 is\nplanning. Do not launch another master or edit controller files while it is\nactive. Poll the session and consult current state before resuming. This is\na dated checkpoint; saved state and events record subsequent changes.\n\n```text\npython3 /home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/scripts/run_accounting_master.py status\n```\n\nAfter this invocation exits, resume with:\n\n```text\npython3 /home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/scripts/run_accounting_master.py run\n```\n\nThe current invocation has the configured 7,200-second wall limit, sequential\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '60,156p' docs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md\nsed -n '78,79p' docs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '60,156p' docs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md\nsed -n '78,79p' docs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md\"","aggregated_output":"### G12. Cross-company concepts and aggregation need formal mapping semantics\n\nRequirements: MC02, MC06, MC07, MC20, MC24. Refines G2, G4 and G7.\nEvidence: [concept relationships](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/02-history.tex:54)\nand [contextual aggregation](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/06-language.tex:69).\n\nEquivalent, component, broader, reclassified and measurement-transformed\nconcepts are named, and partitions are required. Their records, applicability\nconditions and allowed compositions are not fully defined. There is no worked\ncase showing company extensions changing over time, gross/net distinctions,\nor two classifications of the same revenue that must not be summed together.\n\nRequired evidence: a mapping registry and application rules, with cases where\nsimilar labels mean different measurements and different labels mean the same\nquantity. Define what proves a partition disjoint/exhaustive, how unallocated\nresiduals are represented and how perimeter/context changes affect mappings.\nThe representation need not impose one universal chart of accounts, but it\nmust specify how comparability is established or left unresolved.\n\n### G13. Multiple clocks are identified without complete historical query rules\n\nRequirements: MC05, MC19, MC25. Refines G2, G4 and G10.\nEvidence: [time and views](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/02-history.tex:80)\nand [EvidenceView](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/11-contracts.tex:92).\n\nStoring dates and supersession links does not specify which assertion wins a\nquery. The design needs precise rules for incomplete publication timestamps,\nconflicting available filings, selective restatements, changed accounting\nbases and calendars, and different investor-information versus system-version\nqueries. Prospective estimate changes and retrospective corrections are\ndelegated to future packages without a complete transition example.\n\nRequired evidence: a multi-date example with explicit publication, ingestion,\neconomic and reporting times, original and revised amounts, and the exact\nrecords/results returned by each supported view. Show invalid year-to-date\nsubtractions across revisions as well as a valid one. Declare unsupported\ntiming assumptions rather than silently using the latest available row.\n\n### G14. Scenario modes and permitted information need enforceable contracts\n\nRequirements: MC14, MC18. Refines G6 and crosses modelling/execution requirements.\nEvidence: [three scenario meanings](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/03-literature.tex:149),\n[information timing](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/05-mathematics.tex:121),\nand [scenario grammar](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/11-contracts.tex:51).\n\nThe literature chapter promises to distinguish an imposed exogenous path,\nan observational conditional forecast and an intervention. The surface example\nonly sets a driver. The record/API specification does not supply complete\nmode-specific semantics for conditioning or replacing equations. Similarly,\nbehavioural and measurement plugins are told to use permissible information,\nbut the available-information object and its access rules are unspecified.\n\nRequired evidence: declare supported scenario kinds and represent them in the\nschema. A first release can explicitly support exogenous stress only without\nclaiming the other operations. Show how a manager and an allowance calculation\nreceive current information while future simulated outcomes remain hidden.\nExplain when new observed evidence updates historical weights and why merely\nselecting a hypothetical stress does not do so.\n\n### G15. Different kinds of uncertainty need different admissibility rules\n\nRequirements: MC04, MC08, MC10, MC12, MC24. Refines G1, G2 and G6.\nEvidence: [interpretation distinction](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/01-purpose.tex:67)\nand [alternative records](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/06-language.tex:183).\n\nAn unknown fixed-rate share, two readings of a note, a permitted accounting\nelection, a measurement estimate and a future management decision are different\nuncertainties. The text recognises this, but generic symbols/choices and\nassumption provenance do not fully specify how each kind is validated,\nupdated or propagated. An unsupported treatment must not be accepted as an\nequally legitimate interpretation merely because it produces balanced entries.\n\nRequired evidence: define these distinctions in the model and review contracts,\nincluding links between dependent uncertainties. Show an admissible alternative,\nan evidence-refuted alternative and an unsupported accounting treatment.\nPreserve a possibly erroneous source assertion as evidence without silently\nendorsing its treatment. This requires no new fraud-detection product.\n\n### G16. Aggregation and history compression need a practical resolution policy\n\nRequirements: MC11, MC22. Refines G1 and G6.\nEvidence: [conditional-law equivalence](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/05-mathematics.tex:222).\n\nThe definition that grouped histories must have the same relevant conditional\nlaws is useful. It does not supply a usable rule for choosing instrument,\nlot, vintage or cohort resolution, carrying necessary accounting memory, or\nreconsidering a grouping when a scenario/horizon changes. The draft correctly\navoids claiming a general equivalence-deciding compiler, but does not specify\nenough supported transformations in its place.\n\nRequired evidence: define resolution metadata, state requirements and a small\nset of justified transformations. Include one grouping that preserves the\nrequested results and another that loses a rate, maturity or guarantee\nexposure. Declare the scope/error of approximate aggregation and retain its\nsource/detail references. Changing the query must trigger a sufficiency check.\n\n### G17. Local evidence review needs a state machine and invalidation rules\n| MC14 | Give scenarios and decision information explicit meanings. U2, P, D. | Define supported exogenous stress, observational-conditioning and intervention modes, or explicitly scope unsupported modes; enforce information dates and distinguish real-world from pricing measures. | Specified exogenous stress, observational conditioning, intervention preconditions and information capabilities in Ch. 8/Core 0. Finite conditioning, an information-date example and debt stress typing/provenance are checked; causal intervention execution and arbitrary information-policy enforcement remain pending. G6, G14. |\n| MC15 | Specify ordinary corporate operations and accounting across periods. U1, U2, U3, D. | Provide a bounded coherent package for revenue/collections, purchases/payments, inventory/costs, assets/depreciation, payroll, financing and applicable closing/tax assumptions, with explicit exclusions. | Specified bounded corporate package in Chs. 2, 8 with exact annual/interim and forecast fixtures. Delivery, collection, purchase, payment, costs, plant, payroll, debt, simple tax and closing reconcile. Real tax/revenue/lease/FX packages remain separate work. G4, G5. |\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
