{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,25p' docs/plans/accounting-product-design-checkpoint.md\nsed -n '1,25p' data/accounting-master/next-plan.md\nsed -n '1,35p' docs/design/spec/reconstruction-profile-v1.md\nsed -n '160,181p' scripts/core_semantics.py\"","aggregated_output":"# Active checkpoint\n\nUpdated: 2 October 2026 (Asia/Hong_Kong), after multi-year source-corpus\nacceptance following the expanded-audit repair. The user directed us to do all\nfeasible internal work before costly professional review. MC35 preserves that work order.\nThe wider mission remains active; human review is not the next automatic step.\n\n## Accepted source corpus and next execution\n\nThe user's corpus-first work unit is complete at the source-acquisition layer:\n**192 of 192 target reports, 2018–2025, across nine issuers and three evidenced\naccounting families. All nine have eight consecutive complete years.**\n`target-panel-v2.json` is active and is now the collector's explicit default.\nHenkel replaces Unilever and Munich Re replaces Allianz under the reviewed\nsource-access repair; frozen v1 coverage and all original files remain under\n`data/financial-report-benchmark/snapshots/`.\n\nResume from the [corpus result](accounting-benchmark-corpus-results.md),\n`data/financial-report-benchmark/index.html`, `coverage.json` and\n`integrity-manifest.json`. QA 6 revalidated all 244 retained original versions;\nthe independent hash/provenance/grid/PDF checks pass, and 20 regression tests\npass. The old 12-, 157- and 159-report counts are historical. There are 738\nattempt/revalidation records, not 738 benchmark observations.\n\nThe collector checkpoints each attempt and supports `--revalidate-retained`,\n# Accounting master — refreshed next plan\n\nUpdated: 2026-10-03T00:07:09.673479+00:00\n\nNext eligible phase: P05.\nMission complete: **no**. Scoped phase acceptance does not close the original gaps.\n\n| Phase | State | Residual work |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| P00 — Verify the accepted baseline | accepted_internal | All G1–G18 retain work; bounded reference checks do not establish accounting or forecast validity. |\n| P01 — Prepare source-context and availability work records | accepted_internal | Publication/version evidence, semantic annotation, incorporated packages and benchmark labels remain open. |\n| P02 — Complete the bounded Apple case preparation | accepted_internal | The previous structured review returned AGREE, but its process record reports timeout; supervisor acceptance remains pending.; Complete note semantics, remaining indentures, series certificates and omitted instruments remain unresolved through specific recorded source routes.; Historical retained-byte availability and whole-document representation equivalence remain unestablished.; Debt/swap allocation, noncash movements, asset cohorts and contingent outcomes remain unidentified.; Selected identities do not establish full accounting validity, empirical forecast validity or human acceptance. All G1–G18 retain wider obligations.; Two temporary-file tests could not be independently rerun in this read-only environment; their passing status relies on the matching supervisor check record and inspected test code.; Complete agreement semantics, remaining indentures, series certificates and omitted instruments remain unresolved through specific recorded source routes.; Historical availability of retained bytes and whole-document representation equivalence remain unestablished.; Selected reconciliations establish neither full-company accounting validity nor empirical forecast validity. Human acceptance remains pending; all G1–G18 retain wider obligations.; This review changed no files. |\n| P03 — Implement source lowering and shared IR | accepted_internal | General language support, arbitrary and cross-company mappings, and broader uncertainty remain incomplete; G2, G12 and G15 remain open.; Accounting validity, empirical forecast validity, authoring superiority and human acceptance are not established.; Git provenance remains unavailable; recorded content hashes provide file provenance.; General package loading and overrides, events, postings, journals, runtime execution, arbitrary mappings, multiple entities/books/observations, currencies/calendars, cross-company mappings and broader uncertainty remain unsupported.; In-place checker execution was blocked by the read-only workspace; the same checker passed in a disposable writable copy with only expected temporary-path and timing differences. |\n| P04 — Implement reconstruction and numerical operations | accepted_internal | Independent acceptance remains pending; the previous timed-out review does not establish acceptance.; Arbitrary-history completeness, nonlinear inference, continuous probabilistic inference, unbounded integer search and general aggregation equivalence remain unsupported.; Accounting validity, empirical forecast validity and human acceptance remain unestablished. MC01–MC35 and G1–G18 retain wider obligations.; Four P04 checker tests and two P03 checker tests were not independently rerun in this read-only review; their passing status relies on matching recorded checks and inspected test code.; Template discovery, arbitrary-history completeness, nonlinear inference, continuous probabilistic inference, unbounded integer search and general aggregation equivalence remain unsupported.; Admission records do not establish evidence truth or professional accounting eligibility.; Accounting validity, empirical forecast validity and human acceptance remain unestablished; MC01–MC35 and G1–G18 retain wider obligations.; This review changed no files. |\n| P05 — Execute the bounded company path | needs_repair |  |\n| P06 — Enforce context, chronology and resolution | running |  |\n| P07 — Implement review, persistence and recovery | pending |  |\n| P08 — Resolve authority and corporate-method obligations | needs_repair |  |\n| P09 — Extend bank methods | pending |  |\n| P10 — Extend insurance methods | pending |  |\n| P11 — Exercise adapters and matched frontends | pending |  |\n| P12 — Prepare and exercise a bounded benchmark | pending |  |\n| P13 — Develop calibrated forecasting methods and evidence | pending |  |\n| P14 — Integrate the design and independent-review preparation | pending |  |\n\n# Bounded reconstruction v1\n\nThis executable profile addresses MC08–MC12, MC18 and MC26. It constructs a joint\nfamily from declared templates, slots, openings, dated mappings and admitted\nobservations. It does not discover templates or infer arbitrary company histories.\n\n## Pre-execution research intent and evidence contract\n\nQuestion: do declared inputs generate the correct family within their finite\nscope? Mechanism: rational linear constraints with shared economic identifiers,\nexplicit finite choices and bounded integer domains. Expected failure modes are\nlost dependence, wrong strict endpoints, unexamined rounding and false completeness.\nComparators are an independent Fraction replay/enumerator over original fixtures\nand analytic continuous bounds. Exact feasible-set equality and endpoint proofs\nare pass criteria. Unsupported operations, unknown backend replies, unfinished\ncells or unresolved matching obligations veto exact certification. Corrupted\ninputs or protection failures veto acceptance and stop the checker. A numerical\nfailure triggers repair, not rejection of the research direction. Runtime is\nexplanatory only. No superiority, general accounting validity, forecast validity,\ncontinuous probabilistic inference or human acceptance follows from these checks.\nConformance JSON and result.md preserve results; progress.md is a reset checkpoint.\n\nSkeptical audit: the earlier ambiguity between named views and search choices is\nresolved explicitly below. Baselines use original inputs, not generated expected\nanswers. Fixture sizes and budgets are engineering choices. No stochastic ranking\nor production-default promotion is attempted. A successful command can still be\nmisleading if both construction and oracle share lowering; the oracle therefore\nreplays postings independently. The integration checks inspect the unnamed\ninterior, not only endpoint extrema.\n\n## Assumptions and defaults\n\n| Choice | Provenance/status | Justification | Failure mode / early diagnostic |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Fraction arithmetic | Core contract, reviewed requirement | exact disclosed decimals | binary-float drift; reject floats |\n                require(not d['values'], 'InvalidDomain', where, 'Numeric interval has no finite-value payload')\n                require(low is None or high is None or low < high or\n                        (low == high and d['lower_closed'] and d['upper_closed']),\n                        'InvalidDomain', where, 'Empty/reversed interval')\n                if d['kind'] == 'exact':\n                    require(low is not None and low == high and d['lower_closed'] and d['upper_closed'],\n                            'InvalidDomain', where, 'Exact domain requires equal closed finite bounds')\n        return low, high\n\n    def merge_context(self, contexts, where):\n        ids = [c for c in contexts if c is not None]\n        if not ids:\n            return None\n        keys = ['entity', 'perimeter', 'basis', 'measurement', 'time', 'unit', 'currency', 'dimensions']\n        first = self.ref(ids[0], {'contexts'})\n        for identifier in ids[1:]:\n            other = self.ref(identifier, {'contexts'})\n            require(all(first[k] == other[k] for k in keys), 'ContextMismatch', where,\n                    'Contexts require an explicit compatible mapping')\n        return ids[0]\n\n    def expression(self, identifier, active=()):\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
