{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_22","type":"agent_message","text":"{\n  \"assumptions\": [\n    \"P06 is a new bounded implementation slice: the recovery record and filesystem both show conformance.json, result.md and tests/test_accounting_p06.py absent. No prior P06 review findings or partial implementation were supplied.\",\n    \"Use existing Core 0 context and evidence semantics, with versioned supplemental records where necessary. Preserve P03/P04 implementations, frozen evidence, controller files and benchmark releases.\",\n    \"Support exact rational arithmetic, Gregorian half-open periods, explicit timezone policies, finite partition populations and simple unhedged bullet-debt resolution. These are declared scope restrictions, not general accounting defaults.\",\n    \"P01 filing dates do not establish availability of the retained document bytes. Unknown publication or byte-vintage evidence remains unresolved.\",\n    \"Planning is read-only. This response supplies the plan; the implementation worker must create files and execute checks.\"\n  ],\n  \"checks\": [\n    \"Context/mapping: test equivalent labels with compatible contexts; identical labels with different measurements; parent/group, perimeter-version, basis, currency, calendar and gross/net mismatches; expired mappings; cycles; unsupported conversions; preservation of disclosed spelling, scale, sign and precision.\",\n    \"Partitions: independently enumerate finite members and check disjointness and exhaustiveness. Test missing members, explicit residuals, duplicates and product/geography totals over the same population. Reject double counting even when each axis separately reconciles.\",\n    \"Chronology: test Original, LatestAvailable and Harmonised; cutoff equality; ingestion cutoff; eligible and ineligible successors; transitive/selective revisions; competing successors; dangling links and cycles; named-timezone next-midnight boundaries; absent timezone; unknown publication and byte vintage.\",\n    \"YTD: independently verify 260 minus revised H1 110 equals H2 150; reject subtraction using incompatible original H1 120. Also reject instant subtraction, different starts, nonnested ends, calendar/context mismatches and an unsupported revision-compatibility declaration.\",\n    \"Uncertainty/information: every supported category gets a positive case and semantic negative cases, including dangling/cyclic dependencies, prohibited election, missing estimate inputs, future-information leakage, invalid joint law and incompatible probability measures. Unknown categories and unsupported scenario modes must fail explicitly.\",\n    \"Resolution: compare individual and grouped exact rational outputs; vary rate, maturity, reset, hedge, horizon, scenario, report set and evidence view. Check stale-result rejection and successful fresh revalidation where appropriate. Approximation must reject absent, stale, understated or out-of-scope error evidence.\",\n    \"Integration: select evidence, map context, derive a period, admit uncertainty and evaluate query resolution through one public entrypoint. Mutate source amounts and revision links to prove input sensitivity; verify that revisions invalidate dependent current results while preserved earlier results remain unchanged.\",\n    \"Execute CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1 python3 -B -m unittest discover -s tests -p 'test_accounting_p06.py' -v, followed by the corresponding commands for test_accounting_p03.py and test_accounting_p04.py. These are deterministic engineering checks, not scientific comparisons.\",\n    \"Execute CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1 python3 -B scripts/check_accounting_p06.py --output-dir data/accounting-master/deliverables/P06 --approved-plan <supervisor-supplied-approved-plan-file> --execution-inventory <supervisor-supplied-pre-edit-inventory-file>. Resolve both supplied paths before execution; missing provenance prevents a passing report.\",\n    \"Require all catalogued obligations observed exactly